# Non-linear matter power spectrum 

In this paper, we employ the fitting formula for the non-linear matter power spectra in the WDM and MDM models based on the CDM one given by (cite: Takahashi:2012em) (and (cite: Inoue:2014jka)). There are 8 parameters, $a_n$, $b_n$, $c_n$, $\alpha_n$, $\beta_n$, $\gamma_n$, $\mu_n$, $\nu_n$ in the formula. We use the same parameters as (cite: Takahashi:2012em) but adopt $a_n$, $c_n$ and $\gamma_n$ from (cite: Inoue:2014jka). The following is a summary of those parameters: $$\begin{align}
&\log_{10} a_n = 0.9221 + 2.0595 n_\mathrm{eff} + 2.4447 n_\mathrm{eff}^2 + 1.2625 n_\mathrm{eff}^3 + 0.2874 n_\mathrm{eff}^4 - 0.7601 C\,,\\[8pt]
&\log_{10} b_n = -0.5642 + 0.5864 n_\mathrm{eff} + 0.5716 n_\mathrm{eff}^2 - 1.5474 C\,,\\[8pt]
&\log_{10} c_n = 0.4747 + 2.1542 n_\mathrm{eff} + 0.8582 n_\mathrm{eff}^2 + 0.8329 C\,,\\[8pt]
&\alpha_n = \bigl| 6.0835 + 1.3373 n_\mathrm{eff} - 0.1959 n_\mathrm{eff}^2 - 5.5274 C \bigr|\,,\\[8pt]
&\beta_n = 2.0379 - 0.7354 n_\mathrm{eff} + 0.3157 n_\mathrm{eff}^2 + 1.2490 n_\mathrm{eff}^3 + 0.3980 n_\mathrm{eff}^4 - 0.1682 C\,,\\[8pt]
&\gamma_n = 0.2247 - 0.2287 n_\mathrm{eff} + 0.9726 C - 0.0533 \ln\biggl(\frac{k}{h\mathrm{Mpc}^{-1}} \biggr) \,,\\[8pt]
&\mu_n = 0\,,\\[8pt]
&\log_{10} \nu_n = 5.2105 + 3.6902 n_\mathrm{eff}\,.
\end{align}$$ Here the effective spectral index $n_\mathrm{eff}$ and the curvature $C$ are defined as $$\begin{align}
n_\mathrm{eff} + 3 = - \frac{d\ln \sigma^2(R)}{d\ln R}\biggl|_{\sigma=1}\,,\qquad C = - \frac{d^2\ln\sigma^2(R)}{d\ln R^2}\biggl|_{\sigma=1}\,,
\end{align}$$ or $$\begin{align}
n_\mathrm{eff} = I_1-3\,,\qquad C = 2I_1 + I_1^2 - I_2\,,
\end{align}$$ where $$\begin{align}
I_1 = \frac{2}{k_\sigma^2} \int \frac{dk}{k}\, k^2 \Delta_\mathrm{Lin}^2(k)\, e^{-(k/k_\sigma)^2}\,,\qquad I_2 = \frac{4}{k_\sigma^4} \int \frac{dk}{k}\,k^4 \Delta_\mathrm{Lin}^2(k)\, e^{-(k/k_\sigma)^2}\,,
\end{align}$$ and the wave number $k_\sigma$ is determined so that $\sigma^2(k_\sigma^{-1}) = 1$. Note that the variance $\sigma^2$ is computed by applying the Gaussian filter. The linear matter power spectrum $\Delta_\mathrm{Lin}^2(k)$ is evaluated by the fitting formula given in (cite: Eisenstein:1997ik).

We obtain the non-linear matter power spectrum $\Delta^2(k)\equiv k^3 P_\mathrm{CDM}(k)/(2\pi^2)$ by substituting the above into the following expression (cite: Takahashi:2012em): $$\begin{align}
\Delta^2(k) = \Delta^2_Q(k) + \Delta^2_H(k)\,,
\end{align}$$ where $$\begin{align}
&\Delta^2_Q(k) = \Delta_\mathrm{Lin}^2(k)\, \Biggl[\frac{\bigl\{ 1+\Delta_\mathrm{Lin}^2(k) \bigr\}^{\beta_n}}{1+\alpha_n \Delta_\mathrm{Lin}^2(k) } \Biggr]\, \exp\biggl(-\frac{(k/k_\sigma)}{4} - \frac{(k/k_\sigma)^2}{8}\biggr)\,, \\[8pt]
&\Delta^2_H(k) = \frac{1}{1 + \mu_n (k/k_\sigma)^{-1} + \nu_n (k/k_\sigma)^{-2}}\, \frac{a_n (k/k_\sigma)^{3f_1(\Omega_m)}}{1 + b_n (k/k_\sigma)^{f_2(\Omega_m}) + [c_n f_3(\Omega_m)\,(k/k_\sigma)]^{3-\gamma_n}} \,,
\end{align}$$ with $$\begin{align}
f_1(\Omega_m) = \Omega_m^{-0.0307}(z)\,, \qquad f_2(\Omega_m) = \Omega_m^{-0.0585}(z)\,, \qquad f_3(\Omega_m) = \Omega_m^{0.0743}(z)\,.
\end{align}$$

